---
title: Privacy & security
description: Why WeLovePDF processes files in your browser and what that means for sensitive documents.
---

WeLovePDF is built around one principle: **your files should stay on your device**.

## No server uploads

When you merge, compress, or sign a PDF on WeLovePDF:

- File bytes are read in your browser
- Processing uses in-memory APIs (PDFium, pdf-lib, and similar libraries)
- Output is generated locally and offered as a download

We do not receive your document contents on our servers for these tools.

> **Network requests:** The website itself loads over HTTPS (HTML, JavaScript, WASM). Analytics (Plausible) records page views, not file contents. Service workers may cache static assets for speed.

## Digital signatures

For **Digital Sign PDF**, your `.p12` / `.pfx` certificate and password are used only in the browser to create a PKCS#7 signature. Private keys are not sent to us.

## Sensitive documents

For highly confidential PDFs:

- Use a trusted device and up-to-date browser
- Close other tabs/extensions you do not trust
- Prefer **digital signing** over plain text signatures when legal proof matters

## Local storage

WeLovePDF may store **recent tool visits** and optionally **recent files** (IndexedDB, on your device only) to improve UX. You can clear recent files from the homepage.
